# rule.always.run-the-razors-before-a-claim

> **before a claim leaves you, put to it the razor its shape invites. each razor's question, and what settles it: `catalog.of=razor._.md`.**

shapes: a cause → occam, anti-razor, hickam, hume-proportion, instrument · a blame or a credit of intent → hanlon, morgan · a rival dismissed → rapoport · a verdict of fact → hitchens, russell · a superlative → sagan · a refutation → duhem-quine · two options as the only two → false-dilemma · an ought → hume-is-ought · no test named → popper, alder · a removal → chesterton · a count as an outcome → goodhart · a sample as the whole → survivorship · "all" over a few cases → hasty-generalization, overfit · a lesson moved to a new place → external-validity · parts said of the whole, or the reverse → composition-division, simpson · a label given a will → misplaced-concreteness · a claim from atop a layer → leaky-abstraction · a model offered as right → box · all forest or all trees → ladder · "surely different" → base-rate · one source → segal · a word of certainty → feynman, cromwell · a lesson → foundation vs application.
then the work its question owes: logic → inspect · observation → read · rivals → name them first.
test: **which razor does this claim's shape invite, and what is left after it?** a survivor is "not yet refuted", never "proved".
nitpick: a claim of a shape in the table that left with its razor unrun · a razor copied into a second brief instead of cited from its catalog file
